@page "/privacy"
@inject TroopInfo Troop

@* Public: linked from every public page's footer and from the Google sign-in consent screen.
   Keep it in step with what the app actually stores (Data/Entities) and who it shares with
   (Azure hosting, Azure Communication Services email, Microsoft/Google sign-in). *@

<PageTitle>Privacy Policy - @Troop.AppName</PageTitle>

<article class="card legal">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="legal-updated">Last updated: October 30, 2026</p>

    <p>@Troop.AppName (the "site", at @Troop.SiteHost) is run by volunteers of @Troop.Name,
        a Scouts BSA troop, to keep track of troop money: reimbursement receipts, scout accounts,
        invoices, fundraisers and donations. This policy explains what information the site keeps, why, and
        what you can ask us to do with it. The site is run by the troop, not by Scouting America.</p>

    <h2>Information we keep</h2>
    <p><strong>Parents and guardians</strong></p>
    <ul>
        <li>Your name and email address, added by a troop leader so you can sign in.</li>
        <li>Which scouts you're linked to.</li>
        <li>Reimbursement requests you submit: the amount, description, and the receipt image or
            PDF you upload.</li>
        <li>Invoices billed to your family and payments recorded against them.</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>Scouts</strong></p>
    <ul>
        <li>Name, rank and patrol, and the scout's account balance and history (fundraiser
            credits, invoices and adjustments). This is entered by troop leaders. Scouts do not
            have accounts and do not sign in.</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>Adult leaders</strong> who sign in to the admin area</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Your name, email address and the account identifier Microsoft or Google provides when
            you sign in with them, when you signed in, and the access level you've been given.</li>
        <li>A record of changes you make, such as approving a reimbursement or issuing an invoice.</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>Donors</strong></p>
    <ul>
        <li>Your name, the gift's amount (or a description and estimated value for donated goods),
            how and when it was given, and anything you asked it to be used for. If you choose, also
            an email or mailing address so we can thank you. A troop leader enters this when your
            gift arrives.</li>
        <li>If you ask to stay anonymous, families never see your name: a gift credited to a
            scout's account shows as "Anonymous donation".</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>For everyone</strong></p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Sign-in codes:</strong> stored only in scrambled (hashed) form, valid for 10
            minutes, and deleted once used or expired.</li>
        <li><strong>Email log:</strong> for each email the site sends, who it went to, the subject,
            when, and whether it was delivered. The contents of emails are not kept.</li>
        <li><strong>Technical logs:</strong> our hosting provider may record standard technical
            details such as IP address and browser type to keep the site running and secure.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How we use it</h2>
    <p>Only to run the troop's finances: letting you sign in, handling reimbursements and
        invoices, keeping scout accounts, recording and acknowledging donations, and sending the emails described on the site (sign-in
        codes, receipt and invoice notices, and access notices to leaders). We don't sell your
        information, show ads, or use it for marketing.</p>

    <h2>Cookies</h2>
    <p>The site uses only the cookies it needs to work: one that keeps you signed in (12 hours
        for parents, 8 hours for leaders) and security cookies that protect forms. There are no
        analytics, advertising or tracking cookies.</p>

    <h2>Signing in with Microsoft or Google</h2>
    <p>Adult leaders can sign in with a Microsoft or Google account. When you do, the site receives
        your name, email address and an account identifier. It never sees your password and
        doesn't get access to your email, files or contacts. Signing in on its own grants nothing:
        a troop administrator has to give you access first.</p>

    <h2>Who can see it</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Troop leaders</strong> given access to the admin area can see the troop's
            financial records. Parents and guardians see only their own requests, their family's
            invoices and their linked scouts' accounts.</li>
        <li><strong>Service providers</strong> that run the site for us: Microsoft Azure (hosting,
            database, file storage and email delivery), and Microsoft or Google when you choose to
            sign in with them. They handle the information only to provide those services.</li>
        <li><strong>When required by law</strong>, or to protect the troop, its members or the
            site.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Where it's stored and how long</h2>
    <p>Everything is stored in Microsoft Azure data centers in the United States. We keep
        financial records for as long as the troop needs them for its accounting. Nightly
        backups are kept for 14 days. Sign-in codes last 10 minutes.</p>

    <h2>How we protect it</h2>
    <p>The site is served only over encrypted connections (HTTPS), and Azure encrypts stored data.
        Receipts are never publicly reachable: every download checks who is asking. Admin access
        is limited to leaders an administrator has approved, with read-only or edit roles.</p>

    <h2>Your choices</h2>
    <p>You can ask to see, correct or delete the information we hold about you or your scout by
        emailing <a href="mailto:@Troop.ContactEmail">@Troop.ContactEmail</a>. We'll respond
        within a reasonable time. Some financial records, such as completed reimbursements and
        payments, may need to be kept for the troop's accounting even after you leave the troop.</p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>The site is for adults. Children can't create accounts or sign in. Information about
        scouts is entered by troop leaders and is used only to manage their troop accounts. A
        parent or guardian can ask to review or correct their scout's information at any time.</p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>If we change this policy, we'll update the date at the top of this page. Significant
        changes will also be shared with families through the troop's usual channels.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions about this policy or your information: <a href="mailto:@Troop.ContactEmail">@Troop.ContactEmail</a>.</p>

    <p class="legal-links"><a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a> &middot; <a href="/">Back to @Troop.AppName</a></p>
</article>
